What it is for
--------------
Writing Discuss threads back into a COPY of a PDF as standard annotations, so
somebody who only has Acrobat can read the conversation. pdf.js (the other
vendored library here) reads PDFs and cannot write them; this one writes.

Why this build, and not the ESM one
-----------------------------------
`dist/pdf-lib.min.js` is UMD, which is the only shape that serves BOTH callers
from one file: `pdf/viewer.js` loads it as a classic script (it sets
`window.PDFLib`) and `test/pdf-annot.test.mjs` require()s the very same file
through createRequire. The ESM build would have needed a second copy under an
`.mjs` name for node's extension-based module detection, and two copies of a
library is two versions waiting to happen.

Loaded ON DEMAND. `pdf/viewer.js` injects it the first time somebody exports —
half a megabyte is not worth spending on every PDF that is merely read.

Nothing is fetched at runtime: MV3 forbids remote code, and an export that
needs the network is not an export. Checked for `eval` / `new Function` before
vendoring (there are none — the extension page's CSP would refuse them).

Upgrading
---------
Download the tarball for the new version, copy `dist/pdf-lib.min.js` and
`LICENSE.md` (as LICENSE), update the version and the sha256 above, and re-run:
    node frontends/plugin/test/pdf-annot.test.mjs
    node frontends/plugin/test/pdf-render.test.mjs
